__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ruff_cache/

# ─── Node / Next.js ────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
npm-debug.log*
.vercel

# ─── Editors / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# ─── Docs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `docs/` as a whole used to be ignored. That also hid PLAN, API, MCP, AUTH,
# VECTORS, MANUAL, TODO and CONTINUE — every file README.md links to — so a
# clone had broken links and none of the reasoning travelled with the code.
# Only Jelena's private material is excluded now.
docs/jelena/
# Infrastructure plans for Jelena's own machines — her home network, what runs
# on it, how it is exposed. Private, but NOT off-limits: unlike docs/jelena/
# these were written for a future session to execute, so they must stay
# readable. That is the whole reason they are here and not there.
docs/ops/
# other_agent.md is deliberately NOT listed: it is already tracked, so a rule
# here would do nothing but mislead. It is excluded from the *public* repo by
# the sync script instead — see docs/DEPLOY-HF.md.